/    OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM        P?S PAL V08I    11-JAN-15  PAGE 1

    1                /       OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM
    2   
    3                /       OS/8 TO P?S/8 OR P?S/8 TO OS/8 ASCII FILE CONVERSION PROGRAM.
    4   
    5                /       LAST EDIT:      15-APR-1986     11:00:00        CJL
    6   
    7                /       MUST BE ASSEMBLED WITH '/J' SWITCH SET.
    8   
    9                /       P?S/8 UTILITY TO CONVERT ASCII FILES BETWEEN OS/8 MEDIA AND P?S/8 MEDIA.
   10   
   11                /       ANY FILE REPRESENTABLE IN P?S/8 SIX-BIT ASCII SUBSET WITH OR WITHOUT LINE
   12                /       NUMBERS CAN BE CONVERTED TO THE CORRESPONDING SEVEN-BIT ASCII FILE IN OS/8
   13                /       FORMAT IN A MANNER COMPATIBLE WITH OS/8 DIRECTORY CONVENTIONS. THE PROGRAM
   14                /       CAN ALSO BE USED TO REGROUP P?S/8 FILES OR REMOVE/RESTORE P?S/8 LINE NUMBERS
   15                /       FROM A GROUP OF FILES FOR EDITING OR REFERENCE PURPOSES.
   16   
   17                /       PROGRAM OPERATION AND OPTIONS.
   18   
   19                /       CONVERSION OF OS/8 INPUT TO P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES:
   20   
   21                /       .R OS8CON [LIST OF P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES] < (OPTION SWITCHES)
   22   
   23                /       OR
   24   
   25                /       .R OS8CON > [LIST OF P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES] (OPTION SWITCHES)
   26   
   27                /       CONVERSION OF P?S/8 INPUT FILES TO A SINGLE OS/8 OUTPUT FILE:
   28   
   29                /       .R OS8CON [LIST OF P?S/8 INPUT FILES] (OPTION SWITCHES)
   30   
   31                /       THE DIRECTION OF CONVERSION IS DETERMINED BY PASSED P?S/8 FILES BEING EITHER
   32                /       INPUT OR OUTPUT. OS8CON CANNOT BE USED WITHOUT PASSED P?S/8 FILES.


/    OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM        P?S PAL V08I    11-JAN-15  PAGE 2

   34                /       PROGRAM OPTIONS.
   35   
   36                /                       /C      ATTEMPT TO USE MORE MEMORY THAN CURRENT LOGICAL
   37                /                               CORE SIZE INDICATES. OS/8 FILE BUFFERS WILL BE
   38                /                               ENLARGED IN BOTH CONVERSION DIRECTIONS. THIS SWITCH
   39                /                               IS ONLY NEEDED IF THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE IS SET TO
   40                /                               4K EVEN THOUGH MORE IS ACTUALLY AVAILABLE. GENERALLY
   41                /                               CAUSES FASTER CONVERSION TO OCCUR. DEFAULT IF THE
   42                /                               LOGICAL CORE SIZE IS GREATER THAN 4K (I. E. CORE
   43                /                               1-7).
   44   
   45                /                       /E      USE EXTENDED LENGTH P?S/8 OUTPUT FILE PROCESSING
   46                /                               WITHOUT P?S/8 LINE NUMBERS. THE PASSED OUTPUT FILE
   47                /                               SPECIFICATION IS ASSUMED TO BE THE STARTING POINT
   48                /                               FOR OUTPUT FILE CONVERSION LIMITED BY THE DEVICE
   49                /                               LENGTH WORD CONTAINED IN THE EXTENDED USER DIRECTORY.
   50                /                               THE USER IS WARNED TO INVOKE THIS OPTION CAREFULLY!
   51   
   52                /                       /F      DELETE SPECIAL FORM-FEED PROCESSING. THIS CAUSES
   53                /                               OS/8 <FF> CHARACTERS TO BECOME P?S/8 <EOL> SEQUENCES.
   54                /                               P?S/8 <HT> EJECT <EOL> SEQUENCES ARE PASSED LITERALLY
   55                /                               INSTEAD OF CONVERSION TO OS/8 <FF> CHARACTERS.
   56   
   57                /                       /L      OUTPUT <LF> TO OS/8 FILES WHEN PROCESSING P?S/8
   58                /                               <EOL> PRECEDED BY <EOL>. DEFAULT IS TO OUTPUT <CR>
   59                /                               AND <LF>.
   60   
   61                /                       /P      PACK P?S/8 LINE NUMBER FILES. OS/8 <FF> CHARACTER
   62                /                               HANDLING WILL NOT CHECK FOR EXTRA ROOM IN THE FILE.
   63                /                               THIS OPTION IS IGNORED IF /E OR /F IS INVOKED AS
   64                /                               /E USES EXTENDED FILES AND /F DELETES SPECIAL <FF>
   65                /                               PROCESSING.
   66   
   67                /                       /0-/7   LOGICAL UNIT FOR OS/8 INPUT/OUTPUT (DEFAULT IS /7).
   68   
   69                /                       =NNNN   STARTING OS/8 RECORD (DEFAULT IS 0007).


/    OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM        P?S PAL V08I    11-JAN-15  PAGE 3

   71                /       DEFAULT OPTIONS.
   72   
   73                /       OS/8 INPUT/OUTPUT ASSUMES OS/8 RECORD 0007 (P?S/8 BLOCK 0016) ON THE OS/8
   74                /       DEVICE DEFINED BY THE PREVAILING LOGICAL P?S/8 UNIT TO BE USED FOR OS/8
   75                /       INPUT/OUTPUT. THE DEFAULT LOGICAL UNIT IS SEVEN. EITHER OS/8 RECORD OR UNIT
   76                /       CAN BE MODIFIED WITH THE APPROPRIATE EQUALS PARAMETER (FOR RECORD) OR /0 
   77                /       THROUGH /7 (FOR LOGICAL UNIT).
   78   
   79                /       THE OS/8 DEVICE MUST BE LAID OUT IN A MANNER COMPATIBLE WITH P?S/8 BLOCK
   80                /       CONVENTIONS. ALTHOUGH THIS IS USUALLY THE CASE, CONSULT DEVICE HANDLER
   81                /       DOCUMENTATION TO BE SURE.
   82   
   83                /       OS/8 OUTPUT FILE CONSIDERATIONS.
   84   
   85                /       IT IS RECOMMENDED THAT THE OS/8 OUTPUT FILE BE APPLIED TO AN EMPTY DEVICE
   86                /       (IN THE OS/8 SENSE, THE DEVICE CAN BE ZEROED OUT AND THEN A SINGLE FILE CAN
   87                /       BE TRANSFERRED TO IT VIA THIS UTILITY) TO MAKE THE PROCESS OF CONVERSION
   88                /       EASIER.
   89   
   90                /       **** NOTE **** THIS PROGRAM DOES NOT RECOGNIZE OS/8 DIRECTORY CONSIDERATIONS,
   91                /       IT CAN ONLY WRITE THE ACTUAL FILE AS OS/8 WOULD REQUIRE IT ASSUMING THE
   92                /       BLOCK LAYOUT SCHEME IS COMPATIBLE WITH P?S/8 ON THE LOGICAL OUTPUT UNIT.
   93   
   94                /       THIS UTILITY IS IGNORANT OF OS/8 LENGTH RESTRICTIONS AND COULD ATTEMPT TO
   95                /       ACCESS NON-EXISTANT RECORDS OR OVERWRITE RECORDS HIGHER UP ON THE OS/8 DEVICE
   96                /       ORDINARILY BELONGING TO OTHER OS/8 FILES.
   97   
   98                /       BY USING THE DEFAULT OPTIONS, AN OS/8 FILE WILL BE PLACED WHERE IT WOULD
   99                /       BE PLACED BY OS/8 ITSELF JUST AFTER ZEROING THE DIRECTORY. THIS ALLOWS THE
  100                /       FOLLOWING METHOD TO WORK:
  101   
  102                /       (FROM P?S/8)
  103   
  104                /       .R OS8CON,PQSFIL/1=7            CONVERT PQSFIL TO OS/8 FORMAT ON UNIT 0001
  105                /                                       AT RECORD 0007.
  106   
  107                /       (BOOTSTRAPPING TO OS/8)
  108   
  109                /       ASSUMING AN OS/8 SYSTEM WITH NON-SYSTEM DECTAPE:
  110   
  111                /       .R PIP                          INVOKE OS/8 PERIPHERAL UTILITY.
  112                /       *DTA1:</Z                       ZERO THE OS/8 DEVICE ALREADY CONTAINING
  113                /                                       THE CONVERTED ASCII FILE.
  114                /       *DTA1:PQSFIL</I=1000            USE AN EXCESSIVELY LARGE LENGTH VALUE IN
  115                /                                       THE EQUALS PARAMETER, BUT NOT ONE LARGER
  116                /                                       THAN THE DEVICE. THIS WILL ENSURE THE PROPER
  117                /                                       COVERING OF THE CONVERTED FILE.
  118                /       *DTA1:PQSFIL<DTA1:PQSFIL/D/A    THIS WILL REWRITE THE FILE TO THE CORRECT
  119                /                                       LENGTH IN THE OS/8 DIRECTORY ON DTA1:.


/    OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM        P?S PAL V08I    11-JAN-15  PAGE 4

  121                /       CHARACTER CONSIDERATIONS.
  122   
  123                /       ASSUMING /F IS NOT INVOKED, THE FOLLOWING CONVERSIONS APPLY:
  124   
  125                /       OS/8 TO P?S/8 CONVERSION.
  126   
  127                /       OS/8                                    P?S/8
  128   
  129                /       <FF> PRECEDED BY <CR> OR <LF> OR AT
  130                /       BEGINNING OF P?S/8 OUTPUT FILE          <EOL> <HT> EJECT <EOL>
  131                /       <FF> NOT PRECEDED BY <CR> OR <LF>       <HT> EJECT <EOL>
  132                /       <CR> NOT FOLLOWED BY <LF>               <EOL>
  133                /       <CR>, <LF>                              <EOL>
  134                /       <LF> NOT PRECEDED BY <CR>               <EOL>
  135   
  136                /       P?S/8 TO OS/8 CONVERSION (ASSUMING /L IS INVOKED).
  137   
  138                /       P?S/8                                   OS/8
  139   
  140                /       <EOL> NOT PRECEDED BY <EOL>             <CR>, <LF>
  141                /       <EOL> IMMEDIATELY FOLLOWING <EOL>       <LF>
  142                /       <HT> EJECT <EOL>                        <FF>
  143   
  144                /       ALL LOWER-CASE OS/8 INPUT CHARACTERS WILL BE FOLDED TO THE CORRESPONDING
  145                /       UPPER-CASE P?S/8 OUTPUT CHARACTERS.
  146   
  147                /       ALL CONTROL CHARACTERS OTHER THAN <CR>, <LF>, <HT>, <FF> ARE IGNORED.
  148   
  149                /       ALL <RO> CHARACTERS WILL BE IGNORED.


/    OS/8 <- -> P?S/8 CONVERT PROGRAM        P?S PAL V08I    11-JAN-15  PAGE 5

  151                /       CONSOLE MESSAGES.
  152   
  153                /       CANNOT PROCESS MIXED INPUT AND OUTPUT FILES!
  154   
  155                /               P?S/8 FILES MUST BE ALL INPUT OR ALL OUTPUT, NOT BOTH. THE PROGRAM
  156                /               EXITS TO THE MONITOR.
  157   
  158                /       INSUFFICIENT OUTPUT FILES, OS/8 INPUT TRUNCATED!
  159   
  160                /               THE P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES' CAPABILITY WAS EXHAUSTED WITH FURTHER OS/8
  161                /               INPUT PRESENT. THE LAST P?S/8 FILE IS PROPERLY CLOSED AND THE
  162                /               PROGRAM EXITS TO THE MONITOR.
  163   
  164                /       NO P?S/8 FILES GIVEN!
  165   
  166                /               NO P?S/8 FILES (EITHER INPUT OR OUTPUT) WERE GIVEN. THE PROGRAM
  167                /               EXITS TO THE MONITOR.
  168   
  169                /       OS/8 => P?S/8
  170   
  171                /               CONVERSION IS FROM OS/8 TO P?S/8 LINE NUMBER FILES. P?S/8 OUTPUT
  172                /               FILES WERE PASSED WITHOUT /E AND ARE CREATED FROM OS/8 INPUT.
  173   
  174                /       OS/8 => P?S/8 [EXTENDED FILES]
  175   
  176                /               CONVERSION IS FROM OS/8 TO P?S/8 EXTENDED FILES. P?S/8 OUTPUT FILES
  177                /               WERE PASSED WITH /E INVOKED AND ARE CREATED FROM OS/8 INPUT.
  178   
  179                /       P?S/8 => OS/8
  180   
  181                /               CONVERSION IS FROM P?S/8 INPUT FILES TO A SINGLE OS/8 OUTPUT FILE.
  182                /               P?S/8 INPUT FILES NEED NOT CONTAIN LINE NUMBERS AS THEY ARE IGNORED.
  183   
  184                /       XX FILES CREATED
  185   
  186                /               COUNT OF OUTPUT FILES CREATED BY CONVERSION. CAN BE "NO" (IF NO
  187                /               FILES WERE CONVERTED) OR 1 THROUGH 17, THE P?S/8 UPPER LIMIT. THIS
  188                /               QUANTITY WILL ALWAYS BE 1 IF CONVERTING P?S/8 FILES TO OS/8. THIS
  189                /               MESSAGE IS PRINTED BEFORE EXITING TO THE MONITOR.


